// `f` captures itself before its value exists, so its slot in `outer` gets a
// fresh cell (`NewCell`) before the closure is made, and the closure is written
// into that cell. (At the top level `f` would be a global, which needs no
// cell.) What it returns contains itself, which only an `Any` holds.
// compile: analysed
fn outer() { fn f() -> Any { f } }
